I added `EmptyListMessage` and its light/dark preview in `app/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/org/jetbrains/kotlinconf/screens/EmptyListMessage.kt`. I could not compile it: the build failed with "Unable to locate a Java Runtime", so the code is checked by reading only.

```kotlin
@Composable
fun EmptyListMessage(text: String) {
    Box(
        modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),
        contentAlignment = Alignment.Center,
    ) {
        Text(
            text = text,
            style = KotlinConfTheme.typography.text1.copy(textAlign = TextAlign.Center),
        )
    }
}

@PreviewLightDark
@Composable
private fun EmptyListMessagePreview() = PreviewHelper {
    EmptyListMessage("No sessions match your filters")
}
```

Choices I made:
- **Centring:** the message is centred both horizontally and vertically within the space it is given. The `TextAlign.Center` covers multi-line text.
- **Preview:** I used the existing `PreviewHelper` from `ui-components`. It already applies the app theme, the main background, 8 dp padding and 8 dp spacing, so the preview matches your spec without new layout code. `@PreviewLightDark` produces the light and dark variants.
- **Text style:** the text uses the theme's `text1` style and default primary colour.

To confirm it builds, run `./gradlew :app:shared:compileKotlinJvm` on a machine with a JDK installed.
